From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 05:53:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: apple_tristar_charger: Log a BC1.2 detection
 that finds no charging port

A source without a charger signature is granted the 500 mA of a USB 2.0
port. When that happens on a port known to be a charging port, the
primary detection's D- level is the evidence needed: log it.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
index d3a5daa..19a32c6 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
@@ -510,8 +510,10 @@ static int tristar_identify_bc12(struct tristar_charger *chg, unsigned int bank,
 				 epoch, &dm);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-	if (dm < 326 || dm > 899)
+	if (dm < 326 || dm > 899) {
+		dev_dbg(chg->dev, "BC1.2 primary detection: D- %u mV, no charging port\n", dm);
 		return 0;
+	}
 	ret = tristar_mux_sample(chg, tristar_dplus[bank], 2, 10 + 2 * bank,
 				 epoch, &dp);
 	if (ret)
-- 
